# Turbulence and walls (setup plan step 5, 2026-11-01): a 3-D square cylinder (0.1 m, Re about 6.6e3) set up in
# Physics > Setup from the Resolved turbulence template, switched to DES (Spalart-Allmaras DDES), whose walls are resolved
# by default. A short PISO run averages the flow from the automatic start (40 % of the end time): fieldAverage writes
# UMean, UPrime2Mean and pMean. The Run page then shows the walls' actual y+ (the yPlus function object) and, the mesh
# being far too coarse to resolve the wall, says what to change.
budget p95 80 max 600
shell mkdir -p $SB/ws/sqcyl/system && python3 $QC_TESTS/tools/square_cylinder_mesh.py > $SB/ws/sqcyl/system/blockMeshDict && printf 'FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object controlDict; }\napplication pisoFoam;\nstartTime 0;\nendTime 1;\ndeltaT 1;\nwriteControl timeStep;\nwriteInterval 1;\n' > $SB/ws/sqcyl/system/controlDict && cd $SB/ws/sqcyl && bash -c '. "$WM_PROJECT_DIR/etc/bashrc" > /dev/null 2>&1; blockMesh > log.blockMesh 2>&1'
open $SB/ws/sqcyl
click nav:physics
wait-until page Physics
wait 10
assert enabled su-tmpl#3
click su-tmpl#3
wait 10
assert log simulation.ini turbulence = WALE
note LES walls are resolved by default
assert text Automatic (resolved)
click su-appr#3
wait 5
assert log simulation.ini turbulence = SpalartAllmarasDDES
assert text Automatic (resolved)
note no STL: the y+ helper asks for a size
assert text The y+ helper needs the part's size
screenshot $OUT/01_models.png
note Spalart-Allmaras DDES can also take wall functions: the choice stays open
assert enabled su-wall#1
click su-step#2
wait 5
note the symmetry planes come from the patches' names
assert log simulation.ini role = symmetry
note the inlet's turbulence by viscosity ratio
click su-b#0>inlet>in-tspec
wait 3
click text:Viscosity ratio
wait 5
assert widget su-b#0>inlet>in-ratio
assert log simulation.ini turbulence_by = viscosityRatio
screenshot $OUT/02_inlet.png
click su-step#5
wait 5
click su-et
key A ctrl
enter 0.4
wait 3
click su-dt
key A ctrl
enter 0.002
wait 3
note the averaging starts by itself at 40 % of the end time
assert widget su-avgmode#0
assert log simulation.ini averaging_start = auto
screenshot $OUT/03_solver.png
click su-step#6
wait 5
assert text Nothing to fix
click su-check-run
wait-until page Run
wait 10
click run-go
wait-until job running timeout 30
wait-until job finished timeout 600
assert log log.pisoFoam End
assert not log log.pisoFoam FOAM FATAL
assert log system/controlDict fieldAverage
assert log system/controlDict timeStart       0.16
assert file 0.4/UMean
assert file 0.4/UPrime2Mean
assert file 0.4/pMean
assert file 0.4/yPlus
note the walls' y+ on the Run page, and what to change: the cells are far too big to resolve the wall
wait-until widget run-yplus timeout 30
assert widget run-yplus-advice
note the whole advice: on its own line, or in the chip's tooltip in a short chart
screenshot $OUT/04_run.png
